        <headline>red warning - tornado - in effect</headline>
        <description>
At 5:32 p.m. EDT, a thunderstorm capable of producing a tornado, is located over St. Clements. This thunderstorm is moving quickly to the east at 100 km/h. Destructive winds, damaging hail and flooding rainfall are possible.

Locations and nearby areas that could be impacted include: St. Jacobs, Waterloo, Woodside National Historic Site of Canada, Guelph, Aberfoyle, Eden Mills, Morriston, Rockwood

###

This is a very dangerous and potentially life-threatening situation.

Tornado warnings are issued when a thunderstorm is producing or is likely to produce a tornado.
</description>
        <instruction>Take cover immediately if threatening weather approaches. Please consult local media for more information.</instruction>
        <web>https://weather.gc.ca/</web>
